---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const CALENDLY = 'https://calendly.com/russell-decisive/30min';

const team = [
  {
    name: 'Russell Fette',
    title: 'Founder, Chief Financial Officer',
    body: 'Russell Fette runs Decisive Finance and created Financial Rhythms™, the decision rhythm that lets growing companies make every major call from a view built to decide from, on guarantee. Two decades of finance leadership across Microsoft, JPMorgan Chase, and operating companies at every stage. At Pathwright he drove 40% year-over-year revenue growth and quadrupled net income margin without outside capital. That is where Decision-First Finance took shape. BA in Economics from Whitman College (Phi Beta Kappa).',
  },
  {
    name: 'Christopher Koo',
    title: 'Director of Finance',
    body: 'Christopher architects the financial systems that turn a Diagnostic into execution. Senior finance across JPMorgan, Citi, Imprint, and Synchrony before this; credit-portfolio decisions compressed from weeks to days, reporting lag on a $76B banking portfolio cut in half, product, capital, and pricing strategies aligned to recover millions in partnership value. He turns finance from a rearview mirror into a forward system. BA in Financial Mathematics, Lehigh University. Inside a Decisive Finance engagement, Christopher owns the Unit Economics Dashboard, the Product Line P&Ls, and the Scenario Forecast.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Payal Halani',
    title: 'Finance Analyst',
    body: 'Payal runs the financial analysis layer of every Decisive Finance engagement. Inside a Diagnostic, she turns a messy general ledger into a ranked inventory of decisions, in dollars. Inside a Resolution, she maintains the Forward Capital Register, the weekly actuals-vs-prediction reconciliation, and the cross-subsidy map that reveals which products and customers are actually carrying the business. She is the operational constant between Day 1 and Day 90.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Decisive Finance | Decision-First Finance for operating companies"
  description="The team behind Decisive Finance. Decision-First Finance for operating companies, $5M to $50M in revenue. Guaranteed 3x your Diagnostic fee in recoverable value, in 14 days."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>The team behind the Diagnostic.</h1>
      <p class="hero-subhead">
        Most founders and owners look back wishing they had called it differently. Decisive Finance is a small, senior team built for one job: finding the value trapped inside decisions made on numbers that were never built to decide from, resolving them, and installing the rhythm that keeps doing it. <span class="dollar">Guaranteed 3x your Diagnostic fee in recoverable value, in 14 days. Typical 5x to 10x.</span>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-eyebrow">The team</span>
      <h2>Three people. One job.</h2>
      <div class="team-grid">
        {team.map((member) => (
          <article class="team-card">
            <h3>{member.name}</h3>
            <p class="team-title">{member.title}</p>
            <p>{member.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">Three pillars. One system.</span>
        <h2>This is not a roster of consultants. It is a synchronized team running one playbook.</h2>
        <p class="lede">The decisions weren't wrong. You made them on the only numbers you had, and those numbers were never built to decide from.</p>
        <p>We don't audit the past. We make the next call defensible. Not the generalist who gives you cleaner books. The operator who builds the decision layer your accountant, your bookkeeper, and your monthly reports were never built to give you.</p>
        <ul class="pillars">
          <li><strong>Russell</strong> runs diagnosis and the Three-Path recommendation. He is in every Diagnostic from the Forward Capital Report forward.</li>
          <li><strong>Christopher</strong> runs the forecast and the Decision Package. He owns the output the owner walks into every major negotiation with.</li>
          <li><strong>Payal</strong> runs the dollarization, the reconciliation, and the register. She is the reason the numbers hold up when anyone pushes on them.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Together we install the rhythm the Decisive Finance guarantee measures against. Tier 1 delivers by Day 14 or refunds the fee. Tier 2 delivers the installed rhythm by Day 90 or refunds everything paid to date. Tier 3 runs the rhythm on retainer and certifies Realized Value quarterly.</p>
        <p>You walk into every major decision able to point at the number behind it, and the recovered cash proves the view was right.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="close-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <h2>Start with 30 minutes.</h2>
        <p class="lede" style="color: rgba(255,255,255,0.8);">No pitch. You leave with at least one named action.</p>
        <a href={CALENDLY} class="btn btn-primary">Book 30 minutes with Russ</a>
        <p class="close-tagline">Decide from the numbers. Prove it in the cash.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .team-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .team-card {
    background: var(--white);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 32px 28px;
  }
  .team-card h3 {
    font-size: 22px;
    margin: 0 0 6px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .team-title {
    font-family: Inter, sans-serif;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--orange);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }
  .team-card p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-size: 15px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .pillars {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 28px 0 24px;
  }
  .pillars li {
    padding: 14px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .pillars li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .dollar {
    color: var(--orange);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .close-tagline {
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.6);
    font-size: 15px;
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
